cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "disegreg: shared analysis of solute segregation and defect phases at dislocations in atomistic simulations"
abstract: >-
  disegreg analyses LAMMPS molecular-dynamics / Monte-Carlo snapshots of
  single dislocations in fcc alloys with one common, versioned set of
  definitions (D1, D2). Per run: dislocation lines (OVITO DXA) with exact
  periodic distances in triclinic cells and a structural fallback where DXA
  misses the line, region-resolved solute concentrations, the line excess
  Gamma(R), chemical short-range order, solute clusters, the along-line core
  composition and its spectrum against binomial noise, drift tests and
  block-averaged time averages. Across runs (version 0.2): uptake exponent
  between chemical-potential offsets, McLean prediction from 0 K site
  energies, bottom-up vs top-down hysteresis, the reference composition from
  bulk-control cells with explicit acceptance rules, and a tidy results
  table with provenance and definition status. The bulk-control path and the
  ordered-domain sizes (still a proposal) are tested on synthetic cells only.
  Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research
  Foundation) through Project No. A02 of the SFB 1394 "Structural and
  Chemical Atomic Complexity – From Defect Phase Diagrams to Material
  Properties", Project ID 409476157.
